{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/219118-geist-persona-and-tarot","id":219118,"title":"Geist, Persona, and Tarot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-05T08:47:10-07:00","id":219118,"title":"Geist, Persona, and Tarot","content":"So I did a project a while back that tried to implement the Tarot major arcana of Shin Megami Tensei's Persona series into an alternate way of defining one's threshold and/or archetype. I must've slaved hours over which keys and manifestations each represented, cross-referencing interpretations on what card meant what, and how to translate it into the mechanics given. I didn't want to throw it all away in case someone else could find use for it. If you want, feel free to borrow this, or tell me what you think. I'd love feedback, and would be open to debate on the concept of conversion.<br /> <br /> 0 Fool<br /> Keys \u2013 Phantasmal or Cold-Wind<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Curse, Shroud<br /> <br /> I Magician<br /> Keys \u2013 Pyre-flame or Phantasmal<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Marionette, Rage<br /> <br /> II Priestess<br /> Keys \u2013 Stillness or Stigmata<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Boneyard, Oracle, Shroud<br /> <br /> III Empress<br /> Keys \u2013 Passion or Grave-dirt<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Boneyard, Marionette, Oracle<br /> <br /> IV Emperor<br /> Keys \u2013 Stigmata or Industrial<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Boneyard, Curse, Marionette<br /> <br /> V Hierophant<br /> Keys \u2013 Stillness or Phantasm<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Oracle, Shroud<br /> <br /> VI Lovers<br /> Keys \u2013 Passion or Stigmata<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Marionette, Shroud<br /> <br /> VII Chariot<br /> Keys \u2013 Industrial or Passion<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Curse, Marionette, Rage<br /> <br /> VIII Strength<br /> Keys \u2013 Primeval or Passion<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Marionette, Shroud<br /> <br /> IX Hermit<br /> Keys \u2013 Phantasmal or Stillness<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Curse, Oracle, Shroud<br /> <br /> X Wheel of Fortune<br /> Keys \u2013 Industrial or Grave-dirt<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Boneyard, Curse, Oracle<br /> <br /> XI Justice<br /> Keys \u2013 Phantasmal or Stigmata<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Curse, Oracle, Rage<br /> <br /> XII Hanged Man<br /> Keys \u2013 Stillness or Stygian<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Curse, Oracle<br /> <br /> XIII Death<br /> Keys \u2013 Stigmata or Stygian<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Boneyard, Caul, Curse<br /> <br /> XIV Temperance<br /> Keys \u2013 Phantasmal or Tear-Stained<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Marionette, Shroud<br /> <br /> XV Devil<br /> Keys \u2013 Passion or Stygian<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Boneyard, Marionette, Pit<br /> <br /> XVI Tower<br /> Keys \u2013 Industrial or Stygian<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Curse, Pit, Rage<br /> <br /> XVII Star<br /> Keys \u2013 Passion or Tear-Stained<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Boneyard, Caul, Oracle<br /> <br /> XVIII Moon<br /> Keys \u2013 Primeval or Phantasm<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Curse, Shroud<br /> <br /> XIX Sun<br /> Keys \u2013 Passion or Pyre-Flame<br /> Manifestation \u2013 Boneyard, Caul, Shroud<br /> <br /> XX Judgement<br /> Keys \u2013 Cold-Wind or Stygian<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Caul, Rage, Shroud<br /> <br /> XXI World<br /> Keys \u2013 Passion or Phantasm<br /> Manifestations \u2013 Boneyard, Caul, Shroud<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I also utilized the minor arcana as being factions in Sin-Eater society. It took me a lot of time, but I found a possible interpretation for each of the four.<br /> <br /> Pentacles -- seek to profit from Death<br /> <br /> Cups -- seek to cure Death<br /> <br /> Swords -- seek to combat Death<br /> <br /> Wands -- seek to rule over Death","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T12:13:55-07:00","id":221185,"title":"","content":"Anyone? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T12:49:59-07:00","id":221205,"title":"","content":"I actually think many Sin-Eaters would use the Aleister Crowley version, the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thoth_tarot_deck\" target=\"_blank\">Thoth Tarot</a>.<br /> <br /> If only because I think any don't think any self-aware Sin-Eater is likely to be caught <i>near </i>a card called Temperance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T14:31:16-07:00","id":221270,"title":"","content":"It not so much the tarot card in and of itself, but how the card is tied to death and the hero's journey. Or at least, don't you think?<br /> <br /> Edit: consider each of the tarot given a macabre motif. A geist of Temperance could be an Angelic phantom shaped by the Sin-Eater's actions to match their background and history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 08-07-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T21:18:55-07:00","id":221575,"title":"","content":"that awesome i think ill show this to my players a lot my friends enjoy persona 3 and 4 as well as shin megami.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T04:57:04-07:00","id":221915,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea, though I'm leery of using the Tarot at all in its current state. Just one problem; The Devil lists Stygian as one of its favored keys. While I haven't read Book of the Dead, and from what I've heard it would be thematic, my understanding of things is that Stygian is something indescribably wrong, not something that a Threshold would favor. Sorry if I'm wrong and just wasting your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T05:11:15-07:00","id":221929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/219118-geist-persona-and-tarot?p=221915#post221915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea, though I'm leery of using the Tarot at all in its current state. Just one problem; The Devil lists Stygian as one of its favored keys. While I haven't read Book of the Dead, and from what I've heard it would be thematic, my understanding of things is that Stygian is something indescribably wrong, not something that a Threshold would favor. Sorry if I'm wrong and just wasting your time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point! The Devil is about temptation, and how it binds us to our passions. Each Major Arcana is not just a personification of the Sin-Eater's soul merged with Geist, but also an ordeal they must overcome if they are to unlock their full potential. The Stygian Key and Pit Manifestation aren't normally accessible at character creation, but in this way, they represent how easy it is for people of said-arcana to become corrupted by power. It's all in the narrative of character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}